<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A:default">
<!--
    AArch64 compiler traps (always on).

    Issue: AArch64 SLEIGH lowers `brk #imm16` to
    `pc = SoftwareBreakpoint(imm16, inst_next); goto [pc];`. Jump-table recovery
    cannot resolve that jump, so flow truncated it to a call followed by a
    return, and a function whose overflow or bounds check ends in a compiler
    trap printed as void and passed the value it returns to the trap, or
    returned a value fabricated from a call through the trap
    (`return (*v1)();`).

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 flow classification. `p2_lift/kuna_brktrap.rs` matches
    a BRANCHIND through the result of a `SoftwareBreakpoint` CALLOTHER in the
    same instruction whose immediate a compiler emits for a trap that does not
    return (#1 llvm.trap, #1000 GCC __builtin_trap, #0x5500-#0x55ff
    llvm.ubsantrap, #0xc470-#0xc473 arm64e pointer-auth failure, #0xf003 MSVC
    __fastfail), and `flow.rs` replaces the jump with a no-return halt.

    Bytes assembled with `clang -c -arch arm64` / `clang -target
    aarch64-linux-gnu -c` (each function 16-byte aligned):
      0x100000 add_trap      adds x0,x0,x1; b.vs 1f; ret; 1: brk #1
                             (clang -O2: if (__builtin_add_overflow(a,b,&r))
                             __builtin_trap(); return r;)
      0x100010 mul_add_trap  mul x8,x0,x1; smulh x9,x0,x1; cmp x9,x8,asr #63;
                             b.ne 1f; adds x0,x8,x0; b.vs 1f; ret; 1: brk #1
                             (two checks sharing one trap)
      0x100030 index_gcc     cmp x0,#0xf; b.hi 1f; ldr x0,[x1,x0,lsl #3]; ret;
                             1: brk #1000 (GCC's __builtin_trap)
      0x100050 add_ubsan     adds x0,x0,x1; b.vs 1f; ret; 1: brk #0x5500
                             (clang -fsanitize-trap=signed-integer-overflow)
      0x100060 debug_trap    brk #0xf000; add x0,x0,#1; ret
                             (__builtin_debugtrap, which execution continues past)
      0x100070 debugger_bp   brk #0; add x0,x0,#1; ret
      0x100080 deref_fastfail cbz x0,1f; ldr x0,[x0]; ret; 1: brk #0xf003
                             (MSVC __fastfail)
      0x100090 kernel_warn   brk #0x800; add x0,x0,#1; ret
                             (Linux BUG/WARN, which a WARN resumes past)

    One pass at the default: the checked-arithmetic functions return their
    value, every compiler trap is a statement that ends the flow, and the
    three resumable breakpoints keep the jump-as-call.
-->
